          "guid": "mt7pjitbpqow2zzw",
          "message": {
            "text": "Independent task 288 built the validation headless_shell from a separate output root with the same authenticated GN args; explicit-headless task 289 then retained 38 rows (20 authorized, 18 body-free denied) at the same normalized logical digest as proposal task 287. The two raw files reopen at their recorded SHA-256 values, and the adjudicator report self-hash reopens while withholding only the four DM-2589 Linux/Windows arms—so this proves the macOS pair without overstating a global verdict.",
            "markdown": "Independent task 288 built the validation headless_shell from a separate output root with the same authenticated GN args; explicit-headless task 289 then retained 38 rows (20 authorized, 18 body-free denied) at the same normalized logical digest as proposal task 287. The two raw files reopen at their recorded SHA-256 values, and the adjudicator report self-hash reopens while withholding only the four DM-2589 Linux/Windows arms—so this proves the macOS pair without overstating a global verdict."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/231-authenticated-animated-image-byte-ownership.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 477,
                  "endLine": 491,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "The independently rebuilt macOS validation arm contains the same 38 rows and\n20/18 authorization split, with distinct build, process, observation, and\nbrowser-context provenance. Its artifact SHA-256 is\n`e8333f8e2d19d9cff00eba6e0a4a894f72edc9db48cc935f3ea9a06153c96f08`,\nand it reopens to the same normalized logical SHA-256 above.\n\nThe retained two-arm adjudication file SHA-256 is\n`0d4ce53fa5e5730b5138a75bed4496c7741f51b9b507491aabc7b9c5eb513f26`;\nits canonical report self-hash is\n`6cc9deb0697a4d865b742228b83e4a479279c5c69dab8cff3d3261f41d38706d`.\nIt withholds the global verdict for exactly four absent artifacts: Linux\nproposal/validation and Windows proposal/validation, owned by DM-2589. The\nmacOS pair is a private logical evidence checkpoint, not authorization for the\nstock-CDP or production collectors and not a macOS-only global verdict.\n"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
